    schema_name: str,
    schema_errors: List[SchemaError],
) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Dict[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]]], Dict[str, int]]:
    """Aggregate schema errors into a structured, scope-grouped mapping.

    Produces a nested dictionary of the form::

        {
            "SCHEMA": {error_type: [entry, ...], ...},
            "DATA": {error_type: [entry, ...], ...},
        }

    where each ``entry`` is a dictionary with the keys ``"schema"``,
    ``"column"``, ``"check"``, and ``"error"``. The presence of the top-level
    ``"SCHEMA"`` and ``"DATA"`` keys depends on ``CONFIG.validation_depth``.

    :param schema_name: name of the schema being validated.
    :param schema_errors: collected :class:`~pandera.errors.SchemaError`
        objects.
    :returns: a tuple of the nested error message dictionary and a mapping of
